-TEXT -30,-150,-80 7 0 0 (FROM THE WALL SIDE, BAR UPRIGHT)
-TEXT -30,-162,-80 7 0 FIRST TRY BOTH PINS (2.85 MM FILAMENT,
-TEXT -30,-174,-80 7 0 6.0 TO 6.5 MM LONG, NEVER LONGER) IN
-TEXT -30,-186,-80 7 0 THEIR HOLES IN THE SADDLE FLOOR, THEN
-TEXT -30,-198,-80 7 0 TAKE THEM OUT. BAR UPSIDE DOWN: SLIDE
-TEXT -30,-210,-80 7 0 THE SENSOR ALONG THE TUNNEL ROOF INTO
-TEXT -30,-222,-80 7 0 ITS NEST, MARKED FACE TO THE ROOF. BAR
-TEXT -30,-234,-80 7 0 UPRIGHT: DROP IN BOTH PINS. THREAD THE
-TEXT -30,-246,-80 7 0 (FULL STEPS: SEE README.TXT)
-TEXT 270,-150,-80 7 0 1 (SEEN FROM THE WALL SIDE) FEED THE
-TEXT 270,-162,-80 7 0 SENSOR LEADS UP THROUGH THE SLOT IN
-TEXT 270,-174,-80 7 0 THE CHANNEL ROOF FIRST. THEN SLIDE THE
-TEXT 270,-186,-80 7 0 PLATE OF THE HOOK BAR INTO THE
-TEXT 270,-198,-80 7 0 DOVETAIL CHANNEL IN THE BODY FROM THE
-TEXT 270,-210,-80 7 0 WALL SIDE, TAKING UP THE SLACK IN THE
-TEXT 270,-222,-80 7 0 LEADS FROM INSIDE. THE DOVETAIL
-TEXT 270,-234,-80 7 0 CHANNEL IS A SLOT WITH SLOPING SIDES,
-TEXT 270,-246,-80 7 0 (FULL STEPS: SEE README.TXT)
-TEXT 570,-150,-80 7 0 2 THE BACKPLATE GOES ON THE WALL
-TEXT 570,-162,-80 7 0 FIRST: FOUR NO.8 COUNTERSUNK SCREWS
-TEXT 570,-174,-80 7 0 AND WALL PLUGS, PEGS TOWARD YOU, THE
-TEXT 570,-186,-80 7 0 FIXED END OF THE CATCH TONGUE (THE
-TEXT 570,-198,-80 7 0 SPRINGY STRIP IN ITS FACE) AT THE
-TEXT 570,-210,-80 7 0 BOTTOM. OFFER THE BODY UP 14 MM HIGH
-TEXT 570,-222,-80 7 0 ONTO THE PEGS AND LET IT DROP UNTIL
-TEXT 570,-234,-80 7 0 THE CATCH CLICKS. THE HOOK BAR MUST BE
-TEXT 570,-246,-80 7 0 (FULL STEPS: SEE README.TXT)
-TEXT 870,-150,-80 7 0 3 BUTTON FIRST (5C). FEED THE LOOSE
-TEXT 870,-162,-80 7 0 ENDS OF THE BATTERY CABLE DOWN THROUGH
-TEXT 870,-174,-80 7 0 THE BULKHEAD (THE THICK SHELF ABOVE
-TEXT 870,-186,-80 7 0 THE BATTERY), ONE THROUGH EACH END
-TEXT 870,-198,-80 7 0 NOTCH, PLUG LEFT ABOVE. HOLDER STILL
-TEXT 870,-210,-80 7 0 OUT, IN FRONT OF THE BOX: CHECK
-TEXT 870,-222,-80 7 0 POLARITY WITH A METER (REVERSED
-TEXT 870,-234,-80 7 0 DESTROYS THE BOARD), SOLDER EACH WIRE
-TEXT 870,-246,-80 7 0 (FULL STEPS: SEE README.TXT)
-TEXT 1170,-150,-80 7 0 4 ALL PARTS HOME. THE ANTENNA JACK
-TEXT 1170,-162,-80 7 0 SLID INTO THE SLOT IN ITS SHELF FROM
-TEXT 1170,-174,-80 7 0 THE FRONT, FLANGE UNDER THE SHELF,
-TEXT 1170,-186,-80 7 0 WASHER AND NUT ON TOP. IF NOT DONE
-TEXT 1170,-198,-80 7 0 YET, PUSH THE TIP OF EACH LATCH ARM IN
-TEXT 1170,-210,-80 7 0 THE BOTTOM WALL OUTWARD ONCE (AWAY
-TEXT 1170,-222,-80 7 0 FROM THE INSIDE OF THE BOX) TO BREAK
-TEXT 1170,-234,-80 7 0 ITS BREAKAWAY TAB. LID (100 X 171 MM,
-TEXT 1170,-246,-80 7 0 (FULL STEPS: SEE README.TXT)
-TEXT 1470,-150,-80 7 0 5 FINISHED. THE HANGER BOX IS 171 MM
-TEXT 1470,-162,-80 7 0 TALL IN V9.9: 41 MM WAS ADDED AT THE
-TEXT 1470,-174,-80 7 0 BOTTOM FOR THE CLEANING-MODE BUTTON,
-TEXT 1470,-186,-80 7 0 AND EVERY OTHER FEATURE KEEPS ITS
-TEXT 1470,-198,-80 7 0 PLACE MEASURED FROM THE TOP OF THE
-TEXT 1470,-210,-80 7 0 BOX. THE SIGN HANGS ON THE WIDE BAR
-TEXT 1470,-222,-80 7 0 THROUGH ITS HAND HOLE, 6 X 2 MM N52
-TEXT 1470,-234,-80 7 0 DISC MAGNET (EITHER POLE) OVER THE
-TEXT 1470,-246,-80 7 0 (FULL STEPS: SEE README.TXT)
-TEXT 1770,-150,-80 7 0 5B USB-C CABLE PLUGGED IN AT THE LEFT
-TEXT 1770,-162,-80 7 0 EDGE WITH THE LID ON. A NEW HELTEC
-TEXT 1770,-174,-80 7 0 BOARD RUNS THE DEMO IT CAME WITH: IT
-TEXT 1770,-186,-80 7 0 MUST BE FLASHED WITH THE HANGER
-TEXT 1770,-198,-80 7 0 FIRMWARE FROM THE FIRMWARE FOLDER OF
-TEXT 1770,-210,-80 7 0 THE REPOSITORY (STEPS IN
-TEXT 1770,-222,-80 7 0 FIRMWARE/README.MD) BEFORE THE UNIT
-TEXT 1770,-234,-80 7 0 CAN REPORT ANYTHING
-TEXT 2070,-150,-80 7 0 5C (SEEN FROM UNDERNEATH) CLEANING
-TEXT 2070,-162,-80 7 0 BUTTON. NUT AND BLUE SOCKET OFF.
-TEXT 2070,-174,-80 7 0 BUTTON PART WAY UP THROUGH THE HOLE,
-TEXT 2070,-186,-80 7 0 NUT STARTED FROM INSIDE, SOCKET ON
-TEXT 2070,-198,-80 7 0 WHILE THE BUTTON HANGS LOW (ONCE
-TEXT 2070,-210,-80 7 0 TIGHT, THE SHELF ABOVE LEAVES TOO
-TEXT 2070,-222,-80 7 0 LITTLE ROOM), THEN BUTTON HOME, NUT
-TEXT 2070,-234,-80 7 0 TIGHT. ONLY THE TWO SWITCH WIRES
-TEXT 2070,-246,-80 7 0 (FULL STEPS: SEE README.TXT)
-TEXT 2370,-150,-80 7 0 6 (SEEN FROM BEHIND) THE LID ALONE,
-TEXT 2370,-162,-80 7 0 100 X 171 MM: HOOKS, HINGE TABS,
-TEXT 2370,-174,-80 7 0 BATTERY POSTS, DISPLAY POCKET, PRG AND
-TEXT 2370,-186,-80 7 0 RST FINGER PADS WITH THEIR PUSHER PINS
